\frac{BC}{\sin A} = \frac{AB}{\sin C} \implies \frac{BC}{\sin 30^\circ} = \frac{20}{\sin 45^\circ}
\] Since \(\sin 30^\circ = \frac{1}{2}\) and \(\sin 45^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}\), we have: \[
\frac{BC}{\frac{1}{2}} = \frac{20}{\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}} \implies BC = 20 \cdot \frac{\frac{1}{2}}{\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}} = 20 \cdot \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} = 20 \cdot \frac{\sqrt{2}}{2} = 10\sqrt{2}
\] The length of \(\overline{BC}\) is \(10\sqrt{2}\). </think> <answer> \(10\sqrt{2}\) </answer>

